# Wave W17-O (Ragged Pass): stair pine — a ledge pine in deep warm greens, tiered and compact against the mountain wind, its highlight lifted clear of the turf, on stair turf (ground baked in). The Pass’s own tree — deeper and tighter-crowned than Route 112’s open warm-slope fumepine: the stair’s pines hunker, the slope’s pines spread.
